<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đại La</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dai La</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Đại La was a walled citadel on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>, the seat of Chinese governors of the Tang <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> General to Pacify the South and later of local rulers. It was rebuilt by the Tang general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gao-pian">Gao Pian</a> in the 860s. In 1010 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-thai-to">Lý Thái Tổ</a> moved his capital there and renamed it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thang-long">Thăng Long</a>.</p></div>
